 /*
  * Construct the root directory
  *
+ * registry_dir, if non-NULL, overrides where the sensor registry (the
+ * "registry" subdirectory the ADSP reads calibration data from and writes
+ * new registry entries to, e.g. SNS_REG_INIT's scratch files) is backed by
+ * on the real filesystem. When NULL, the pre-existing behavior is kept: a
+ * read-only snapshot under prefix is used, with only two fixed child names
+ * ("registry" and "sns_reg_version") exposed - new files can never be
+ * created there. When given, the whole directory is exposed as a real,
+ * writable, passthrough mapped directory instead, so the ADSP can create
+ * new registry entries that actually persist.
